sizing_for_a_person:
**Source of the request.** Ren, 31 October: "let's get everything ready before presenting to humans. you can easily read 100k tokens, but we as human can not. please". Its record, sources/15-codex-theory-conversations/2026-10-31-ready-for-human-readers.md, is only on branch aj4-human, not on main at eb3045799.

**Adopted text on main.** WHAT-REMAINS, the release gate's item 6:
- a screen is 150 words, ten minutes 1,100 words (8.5 to 11 minutes) and an hour 6,000;
- each layer states its time where it begins, which READING-BUDGETS defines as within the first 150 words;
- the never-cut list (amendment 1), and the measure "warns and never blocks";
- "Chapters, records and studies have no budget." Experiments are not named. So RF's ten-minute part rests on its own board claim, not on an adopted budget [inference].

**The measure.** kit/measure_layers.py, on aj4-human only (`git show aj4-human:_process/research/2026-10-05-generative-foundation-review/root-foundation/development/aj4-alignment-readers/kit/measure_layers.py`). It counts visible prose and leaves out:
- fenced code, comments and `<sup>`;
- link targets and anchors;
- the `Quote [path]:` and `Source [path]:` prefixes.

It finds fronts by the headings `^## The dossier in ten minutes$` and `^## The map in ten minutes$`.

**Forms on main.**
- **theories/becoming/review/PHILOSOPHY.md.**
  - An italic opening line: who it is for; "No person has reviewed this work. It was written with AI… ([how this dossier was made])".
  - Then `<a id="the-dossier-in-ten-minutes"></a>` and `## The dossier in ten minutes`, in bold-led paragraphs: **The question.**, **Two premises, two roles**, **What is proved** (each claim with its base), **The open question**, **Theses and tests** (as they fell), **What is not claimed.**, **What we ask.**, **How long.** ("This section takes ten minutes. With an hour, read … The whole takes about two hours").
  - Size: 1,067 words by wc. The board gives "1,114 words by AJ4's measure, 15 over the budget, the excess what may not be cut (amendment 1)".
  - "How this dossier was made" sits at the end.
- **development/aj4-alignment-readers/FAILURE-MODE-MAP.md.** An italic line: "AI draft … Not reviewed by a person, and not for release … The first section takes twelve to fifteen minutes; [how this map was made] … is at the end". Then `## The map in ten minutes`, bold-led paragraphs and the table first, and "## How this map was made" last.
- **LOGIC.md.** "**Time, and the one-hour path.** This front, to the first item, takes about ten minutes."
- **On aj4-human,** the ALIGNMENT edition has "The dossier in ten minutes" (1,100 words with the title), then "## The tests, as they fell" (358 words, about three minutes).

**Existing test documents are far over and have no ten-minute part.** LA1c's PREDICTIONS is 9,352 words, LA1b's 5,543, LA2's 4,554, and LA4's DESIGN 7,671.

**Inferred shape for RF's designs.**
- An italic line in the first 150 words: AI-written, not reviewed by a person, nothing frozen or run, the part's time and the whole's.
- Then a `## … in ten minutes` section of at most 1,100 words by the measure. For each test it gives:
  - the question;
  - the law and its standing (theorem and its base, reading, or conjecture);
  - the bridge the test can refute, and that it cannot refute the theorem (as in LA3's "What the test cannot refute");
  - the forbidden case and the controls;
  - what a pass would and would not show;
  - what needs Ren's yes (calls, tokens, time, downloads);
  - what is not claimed.
- Then the details. Review history and provenance go last, moved and not deleted.

records_for_designs:
**A design gets no record.**
- The LA4 design commit (f6d6f9edc) added only the experiment files, the index row, the board row and a source record. Its landing (41f09fc1a) touched the board, DIRECTIVE-INDEX, sources/README.md and the generated manifest.
- RR's TR-RR designs have no record either.
- Rationale: "A record registers a scoped claim".

**Lean about a test's world is the exception.** It gets records like any theorem, after a board claim and a core run. LA4's formal part has the-test-season-meets-the-optimum-laws and a-commuting-learner-drives-no-unread-choice, both recorded-checked. RF's claim is "to land as a documents slot", so no Lean is planned.

**After a run.**
- LA1–LA3, LA1b, LA1c, IN1 and VD1/VD2 made no new record. The outcome went to the chapters' thesis evidence, the 08 §9 theses table, the dossier, and existing records' does_not_show and boundaries. VD1: "No record is made, since no prediction passed."
- SC1 and FC1 got assessment records (reviewed-scoped), with canonical_source their RESULTS.md: fidelity-coders-on-own-and-other-texts and fidelity-of-the-classical-statements.

**RF's records already name their tests** in next_delta:
- what-choices-show-of-an-order (RF1): "a frozen test of the reach on choosers";
- what-readings-fix-of-the-unread (RF2): "A frozen test of the chain on a trained model with cues varied apart from content";
- readers-reading-readers (RF4): "a test predicting when sequential choosers stop reading their own signals";
- a-reading-kept-by-its-update (RF3): "a frozen test intervening on a formation's observations (the plan's TR5)";
- a-revision-that-opens-a-correction (RF6.1): "a frozen institution simulation with three controls (the plan's TR4)";
- a-prediction-read-by-what-it-predicts (RF6.3): "a frozen test of a published forecast's response";
- acts-alike-from-a-model-or-from-an-order (RF-M): "a frozen test separating a model that does not separate from an order that ranks otherwise by informing";
- what-a-course-chosen-through-its-model-does-not-test: "a frozen test predicting when a learner stops trying what its model ranks low";
- when-complying-when-read-is-best (RF7): "a frozen test of whether complying when read follows the value and the rise in being kept (none yet)";
- what-holding-for-a-reading-is-worth (RF-M.2): "a frozen test of whether holding follows the model's two excesses";
- a-reading-informed-and-revalued (RF-M.3): no test named;
- when-no-route-stands-above-a-revision (RR): "a frozen test of whether resistance falls with stated restoration and closing a route moves use to another".

[Inference] A design leaves these fields as they are. A frozen run would later change the records' evidence and boundaries through the workflow.
